   "title": "Mission SEHAT, Green Energy Corridor Phase III and India's NDC",
   "parts": [
    {
     "t": "Mission SEHAT: launch",
     "items": [
      [
       "b",
       "**Mission SEHAT:** Science Excellence for Health through Agricultural Transformation.",
       "CA #70"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Launched:** on 11 May 2026 in New Delhi.",
       "CA #70"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Jointly launched by (ministers):** Jagat Prakash Nadda, Union Minister of Health and Family Welfare, and Chemicals and Fertilisers.",
       "CA #70"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Jointly launched by (ministers):** Shivraj Singh Chouhan, Union Minister of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare and Rural Development.",
       "CA #70"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Jointly launched by (bodies):** the Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR) and the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR).",
       "CA #70"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "Mission SEHAT: objective and framework",
     "items": [
      [
       "x",
       "**Core objective:** convert agricultural progress into measurable health outcomes for the people of India.",
       "CA #70"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Key framework:** Healthy Food, Healthy Farms, Healthy India.",
       "CA #70"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**It seeks to integrate:** (1) agricultural science, (2) nutrition research, (3) public-health policy.",
       "CA #70"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "Green Energy Corridor Phase III: approval",
     "items": [
      [
       "b",
       "**Approved:** 30 September 2026, by the Union Cabinet.",
       "CA #70"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Objective:** strengthen renewable-electricity transmission and add battery-storage capacity.",
       "CA #70"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**What is a Green Energy Corridor?** A network of transmission lines and substations that transports electricity generated by renewable-energy plants to the power grid.",
       "CA #70"
      ]
     ]
    },
