  {
   "sheet": 72,
   "unit": 12,
   "title": "Nepal's Rasuwa Flash Flood 2026, GLOF and BIMSTEC Disaster Plan",
   "parts": [
    {
     "t": "The event and the river system",
     "items": [
      [
       "b",
       "**Nepal's Rasuwa Flash Flood – 2026:** date 26 August 2026.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Location:** Rasuwa district, near the Nepal–China border.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "x",
       "**River system affected:** the catastrophic flash flood struck Lhende Khola → Bhote Koshi → Trishuli River.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Nature:** the flood was debris-laden.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Damage:** it damaged settlements, roads, bridges, hydropower projects and communication networks.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Region:** the event affected a strategically important Himalayan border region.",
       "CA #72"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "Cause and mechanism",
     "items": [
      [
       "b",
       "**Source:** according to the International Centre for Integrated Mountain Development (ICIMOD).",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Step 1:** a slope failure occurred on Langtang Lirung.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Step 2:** it triggered a massive rock–ice avalanche.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Step 3:** the avalanche entered the Lhende Khola catchment.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Step 4:** it generated a debris-rich flood.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Step 5:** the event potentially involved temporary river obstruction or displacement, followed by sudden water release.",
       "CA #72"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "Important observations",
     "items": [
      [
       "b",
       "**Galchhi:** at Galchhi, the Trishuli River reportedly rose approximately 9 metres within 30 minutes.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Monitoring stations:** several monitoring stations were damaged or destroyed.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**First view:** the event was initially considered a possible Glacial Lake Outburst Flood (GLOF) or earthquake-related disaster.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Final identification:** subsequently identified primarily as a rock–ice avalanche-induced cascading hazard, rather than a conventional GLOF.",
       "CA #72"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "India's assistance to Nepal",
     "items": [
      [
       "b",
       "**NDRF:** India deployed NDRF teams in Bihar and Uttar Pradesh.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Tunnel rescue:** it provided specialised tunnel-rescue personnel.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Forensics:** a 19-member forensic team was deployed for DNA identification.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**HADR:** the assistance strengthened bilateral Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Relief (HADR) cooperation.",
       "CA #72"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "Glacial Lake Outburst Flood (GLOF)",
     "items": [
      [
       "b",
       "**GLOF:** occurs when a glacial lake suddenly releases water following the failure of its natural ice or moraine dam.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Glacial lakes:** formed by the accumulation of meltwater from glaciers.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Natural dams:** natural ice or moraine dams can retain large volumes of water.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Failure:** failure of these natural barriers can cause sudden water release.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Effect:** such events can produce destructive downstream flooding.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "h",
       "Important distinction in the Rasuwa event"
      ],
      [
       "t",
       [
        "GLOF",
        "Rasuwa Flash Flood"
       ],
       [
        [
         "Sudden release from a **glacial lake**",
         "**Rock–ice avalanche-induced** cascading hazard"
        ],
        [
         "Triggered by failure of natural ice or moraine dam",
         "Triggered by slope failure on **Langtang Lirung**"
        ],
        [
         "Water released from a glacial lake",
         "Debris-rich flood generated by avalanche entering river catchment"
        ],
        [
         "Conventional GLOF mechanism",
         "Not primarily identified as a conventional GLOF"
        ]
       ],
       "CA #72"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "BIMSTEC: disaster preparedness and coordination",
     "items": [
      [
       "b",
       "**Centre of Excellence:** proposed BIMSTEC Centre of Excellence at Jamnagar, Gujarat.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Action Plan:** a Disaster Preparedness and Coordination Action Plan was among the major approvals mentioned.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**India's role:** India leads the BIMSTEC Security Sector, which covers disaster management.",
       "CA #72"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**BIMSTEC members (7):** Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Myanmar, Nepal, Sri Lanka and Thailand.",
       "CA #72"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
